{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-42054","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69447","text":"Handoff — A.3 closure commit, Relation Identity Kernel 0.1.2"}]},{"id":"blk-42055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69448","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: all eight items of your commit ruling are landed, the battery is green at 782/782, and both pinned `sem-` ids are unmoved. Path A is ready to commit."}]},{"id":"blk-42056","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69449","text":"This memo replaces the 0.1.1 handoff. It is organised as your ruling was: one section per commit item, each stating what was wrong, what the repair is, and which check would catch a regression. Section 9 is the part that needs you — Path B, and two things I decided that I would rather you overturn now than later."}]},{"id":"blk-42057","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69450","text":"The verdict first"}]},{"id":"blk-42058","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"node test/conformance.mjs\n  782 passed, 0 failed  (70 annotated doc blocks of 113 swept, 26/26 capabilities cited)"},{"id":"blk-42059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69451","text":"Pinned ids, re-verified live in the browser after every edit:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-42061","spans":[{"id":"spn-69452","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-42062","spans":[{"id":"spn-69453","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-42060","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-42063","spans":[{"id":"spn-69454","text":"starter world"}]},{"id":"blk-42064","spans":[{"id":"spn-69455","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-67e954cfe3115166b49388366df3f062a46572ba2baf53380f1520f4050b60ae"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42065","spans":[{"id":"spn-69456","text":"pinned fixture"}]},{"id":"blk-42066","spans":[{"id":"spn-69457","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d587c403211e5c7b2b3ebdd316496367429ecfe4a"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-42067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69458","text":"Neither moved. That is not incidental to this commit — items 1, 2 and 3 all change what the adapter "},{"id":"spn-69459","marks":["italic"],"text":"produces"},{"id":"spn-69460","text":", and if any of them had leaked into the spine's preimage those two lines would be different. The suite asserts byte equality between "},{"id":"spn-69461","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWithRelations"},{"id":"spn-69462","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-69463","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWorld"},{"id":"spn-69464","text":" for both fixtures before it runs anything else, so a leak fails loudly and first."}]},{"id":"blk-42068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69465","marks":["code"],"text":"rev-"},{"id":"spn-69466","text":" ids "},{"id":"spn-69467","marks":["bold"],"text":"did"},{"id":"spn-69468","text":" move, as expected and as designed: a revision now carries "},{"id":"spn-69469","marks":["code"],"text":"domain: \"signal\""},{"id":"spn-69470","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-69471","marks":["code"],"text":"texture: \"solid\""},{"id":"spn-69472","text":" where it previously carried "},{"id":"spn-69473","marks":["code"],"text":"domain: \"forge.world.core.v1\""},{"id":"spn-69474","text":" and no texture key. "},{"id":"spn-69475","marks":["code"],"text":"rev-"},{"id":"spn-69476","text":" is unpinned and world-independent by §D8.3; nothing published depends on its value."}]},{"id":"blk-42069","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69477","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-69478","marks":["code"],"text":"domain = signal"}]},{"id":"blk-42070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69479","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-69480","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69481","marks":["code"],"text":"edgeToRelationRevision"},{"id":"spn-69482","text":" wrote "},{"id":"spn-69483","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact.profile_id"},{"id":"spn-69484","text":" — the string "},{"id":"spn-69485","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.core.v1"},{"id":"spn-69486","text":" — into the "},{"id":"spn-69487","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-69488","text":" slot."}]},{"id":"blk-42071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69489","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-69490","text":" §D8's field table says a domain is a "},{"id":"spn-69491","marks":["italic"],"text":"profile-declared namespace"},{"id":"spn-69492","text":": "},{"id":"spn-69493","marks":["code"],"text":"signal"},{"id":"spn-69494","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69495","marks":["code"],"text":"digital"},{"id":"spn-69496","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69497","marks":["code"],"text":"mobility"},{"id":"spn-69498","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69499","marks":["code"],"text":"electrical"},{"id":"spn-69500","text":". A profile "},{"id":"spn-69501","marks":["bold"],"text":"declares"},{"id":"spn-69502","text":" domains; it is not one. And §D8.8's own recovery table already fixed the value for the frozen route at "},{"id":"spn-69503","marks":["code"],"text":"domain = signal"},{"id":"spn-69504","text":" — so the adapter was contradicting a normative table sitting 300 lines away in the same document."}]},{"id":"blk-42072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69505","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-69506","text":" A declared map, not an expression:"}]},{"id":"blk-42073","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const PROFILE_DEFAULT_DOMAIN = deepFreeze({ \"forge.world.core.v1\": \"signal\" });\nexport function profileDefaultDomain(profileId)   // → WRL_UNKNOWN_PROFILE_DOMAIN"},{"id":"blk-42074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69507","text":"An unknown profile is refused rather than defaulted, because defaulting is how the original defect would come back."}]},{"id":"blk-42075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69508","marks":["bold"],"text":"Consequence I did not expect, and want you to look at."},{"id":"spn-69509","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69510","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-69511","text":" moved out of the "},{"id":"spn-69512","marks":["bold"],"text":"free"},{"id":"spn-69513","text":" row of the field partition and into "},{"id":"spn-69514","marks":["bold"],"text":"no V1 form"},{"id":"spn-69515","text":". It had been filed free on the reasoning \"a V1 edge writes no domain, so changing one cannot disturb the id\" — true, and irrelevant. A V1 edge writes no domain because it is "},{"id":"spn-69516","marks":["italic"],"text":"entirely"},{"id":"spn-69517","text":" a signal-domain encoding; its two kinds are the two kinds of that one domain. An "},{"id":"spn-69518","marks":["code"],"text":"electrical"},{"id":"spn-69519","text":" relation is therefore not a relation whose domain V1 forgets to mention, it is one V1 "},{"id":"spn-69520","marks":["bold"],"text":"cannot represent"},{"id":"spn-69521","text":" — exactly like an "},{"id":"spn-69522","marks":["code"],"text":"acausal"},{"id":"spn-69523","text":" one. So the projection now refuses it, and the partition reads:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-42077","spans":[{"id":"spn-69524","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-42078","spans":[{"id":"spn-69525","text":"fields"}]},{"id":"blk-42079","spans":[{"id":"spn-69526","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-42076","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-42080","spans":[{"id":"spn-69527","text":"names it"}]},{"id":"blk-42081","spans":[{"id":"spn-69528","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-69529","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69530","marks":["code"],"text":"endpoints"}]},{"id":"blk-42082","spans":[{"id":"spn-69531","text":"2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42083","spans":[{"id":"spn-69532","text":"free"}]},{"id":"blk-42084","spans":[{"id":"spn-69533","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"}]},{"id":"blk-42085","spans":[{"id":"spn-69534","text":"1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42086","spans":[{"id":"spn-69535","text":"no V1 form"}]},{"id":"blk-42087","spans":[{"id":"spn-69536","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-69537","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69538","marks":["code"],"text":"orientation"},{"id":"spn-69539","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69540","marks":["code"],"text":"texture"},{"id":"spn-69541","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69542","marks":["code"],"text":"attributes"}]},{"id":"blk-42088","spans":[{"id":"spn-69543","text":"4"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-42089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69544","text":"Four of seven, not three. The spec's numeric claim was updated to match."}]},{"id":"blk-42090","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69545","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-69546","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69547","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/only-the-key-names-the-relation"},{"id":"spn-69548","text":" (partition, mutating each field in turn and classifying the result), "},{"id":"spn-69549","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/revision-field-partition-is-total"},{"id":"spn-69550","text":" (the partition covers "},{"id":"spn-69551","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-69552","text":" exactly), "},{"id":"spn-69553","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/the-import-supplies-only-declared-constants"},{"id":"spn-69554","text":" (asserts the resolved domain is "},{"id":"spn-69555","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-69556","text":" the profile id — the specific defect, named)."}]},{"id":"blk-42091","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69557","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-69558","marks":["code"],"text":"texture = solid"},{"id":"spn-69559","text":", and directed-texture enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-42092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69560","text":"You rejected my decision #1 with \"V1 semantically implies "},{"id":"spn-69561","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-69562","text":"; restore and enforce it.\" Implemented, and you were right for a reason I had not seen."}]},{"id":"blk-42093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69563","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-69564","text":" The adapter emitted no "},{"id":"spn-69565","marks":["code"],"text":"texture"},{"id":"spn-69566","text":" key. My argument: a missing key and a "},{"id":"spn-69567","marks":["code"],"text":"texture: null"},{"id":"spn-69568","text":" are different claims, and no V1 world ever "},{"id":"spn-69569","marks":["italic"],"text":"considered"},{"id":"spn-69570","text":" texture, so inventing one would put an authored-looking value in an artifact that never carried it."}]},{"id":"blk-42094","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69571","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-69572","text":" That argument answers "},{"id":"spn-69573","marks":["italic"],"text":"may the adapter invent a value?"},{"id":"spn-69574","text":" when the question is "},{"id":"spn-69575","marks":["italic"],"text":"what does this encoding mean?"},{"id":"spn-69576","text":" §5 gives V1 exactly one writable texture, "},{"id":"spn-69577","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-69578","text":" solid. So a V1 structural edge does not "},{"id":"spn-69579","marks":["bold"],"text":"omit"},{"id":"spn-69580","text":" a texture, it "},{"id":"spn-69581","marks":["bold"],"text":"elides"},{"id":"spn-69582","text":" one — the same relationship the artifact has to "},{"id":"spn-69583","marks":["code"],"text":"orientation"},{"id":"spn-69584","text":", which the adapter had been restoring all along without anyone calling it authorship. The test is whether the omitted value is "},{"id":"spn-69585","marks":["italic"],"text":"determined"},{"id":"spn-69586","text":", not whether the bytes contain it."}]},{"id":"blk-42095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69587","marks":["bold"],"text":"What the mistake actually cost"},{"id":"spn-69588","text":", which is the part I think is worth keeping on the page: it made "},{"id":"spn-69589","marks":["italic"],"text":"texture required for directed"},{"id":"spn-69590","text":" — a rule §D8.7 "},{"id":"spn-69591","marks":["bold"],"text":"states"},{"id":"spn-69592","text":" — unenforceable, because the kernel's own relations violated it. So the rule got filed as a V2 obligation, and §D8's texture row shipped as one enforced half and one commented half. A table with a commented row has stopped being a table."}]},{"id":"blk-42096","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69593","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-69594","text":" Both halves now come off one declaration:"}]},{"id":"blk-42097","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const ORIENTATION_TEXTURE = deepFreeze({\n  directed: \"required\", symmetric: \"optional\", acausal: \"forbidden\",\n});\nexport const TEXTURES   = deepFreeze([\"solid\", \"async\", \"verified\", \"fault\"]);\nexport const V1_TEXTURE = \"solid\";"},{"id":"blk-42098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69595","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_MISSING_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-69596","text":" is new. "},{"id":"spn-69597","marks":["code"],"text":"projectRelationRevisionToV1Edge"},{"id":"spn-69598","text":" now "},{"id":"spn-69599","marks":["italic"],"text":"elides"},{"id":"spn-69600","text":" a solid texture on the way out and refuses any other — where the 0.1.1 rule was the opposite, "},{"id":"spn-69601","marks":["italic"],"text":"refuse any texture"},{"id":"spn-69602","text":", which round-tripped only because the adapter had never restored one."}]},{"id":"blk-42099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69603","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-69604","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69605","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/directed-carries-a-texture"},{"id":"spn-69606","text":" (missing → "},{"id":"spn-69607","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_MISSING_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-69608","text":", and the well-formed one still accepted — both halves, so a validator that refused everything would not pass), "},{"id":"spn-69609","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/acausal-carries-no-texture"},{"id":"spn-69610","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69611","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/texture-vocabulary-is-the-specs"},{"id":"spn-69612","text":" (asserts §5's "},{"id":"spn-69613","marks":["bold"],"text":"four"},{"id":"spn-69614","text":" and that V1 writes one of them; narrowing the model's enumeration to what the surface can write would delete three guarantee classes while every other texture check still passed)."}]},{"id":"blk-42100","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69615","marks":["bold"],"text":"Test-authoring note."},{"id":"spn-69616","text":" Two acausal specimens were silently testing the wrong rule after this change: they spread a directed "},{"id":"spn-69617","marks":["code"],"text":"base"},{"id":"spn-69618","text":" that now carries "},{"id":"spn-69619","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-69620","text":", so they failed on "},{"id":"spn-69621","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ACAUSAL_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-69622","text":" under names like "},{"id":"spn-69623","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/canonical-order-is-role-then-terminal"},{"id":"spn-69624","text":". The specimen builder now drops an inherited texture for acausal unless the check is deliberately supplying one. And "},{"id":"spn-69625","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/acausal-carries-no-texture"},{"id":"spn-69626","text":" now supplies a "},{"id":"spn-69627","marks":["bold"],"text":"legal"},{"id":"spn-69628","text":" texture, because an invented one ("},{"id":"spn-69629","marks":["code"],"text":"\"braided\""},{"id":"spn-69630","text":") is refused by the vocabulary first and leaves the orientation rule untested. Same class of error as the \"a law about a seam must parse, not grep\" rule."}]},{"id":"blk-42101","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69631","text":"3. Semantic-ID / artifact binding"}]},{"id":"blk-42102","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69632","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-69633","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69634","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveRelations(artifact, semanticId)"},{"id":"spn-69635","text":" took the world id as an argument and trusted it. Callers passed the one "},{"id":"spn-69636","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWorld"},{"id":"spn-69637","text":" had just returned, so it was always right, and it was checked by nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-42103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69638","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-69639","text":" You demonstrated it: an artifact handed over with "},{"id":"spn-69640","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-000…0"},{"id":"spn-69641","text":" beside it minted a complete, well-formed set of relation ids scoped to a world that does not exist. A world-scoped identity is only as scoped as the world id it is scoped "},{"id":"spn-69642","marks":["italic"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-69643","text":", and a value whose meaning depends on an unverified claim travelling next to it has no meaning. The failure is silent — every id well-formed, every round trip green."}]},{"id":"blk-42104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69644","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-69645","text":" The id is "},{"id":"spn-69646","marks":["bold"],"text":"recomputed"},{"id":"spn-69647","text":" from the artifact's own canonical bytes inside "},{"id":"spn-69648","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveRelations"},{"id":"spn-69649","text":"; a supplied "},{"id":"spn-69650","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-69651","text":" becomes a cross-check refused on mismatch ("},{"id":"spn-69652","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_SEMANTIC_ID_MISMATCH"},{"id":"spn-69653","text":"). The recomputed path is the "},{"id":"spn-69654","marks":["italic"],"text":"only"},{"id":"spn-69655","text":" path — there is no faster one to fall back to. "},{"id":"spn-69656","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveLegacyEdgeCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-69657","text":" routes both of its sides through the same checked boundary, so a sealed-looking record carrying a forged id is refused there too rather than only in the single-world path."}]},{"id":"blk-42105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69658","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-69659","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69660","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/a-forged-world-id-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-69661","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69662","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/the-world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"},{"id":"spn-69663","text":" (running with "},{"id":"spn-69664","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-69665","text":" claim gives the same ids — so the two paths cannot disagree and there is no unchecked way in)."}]},{"id":"blk-42106","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69666","text":"4. Explicit V1 source-version validation"}]},{"id":"blk-42107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69667","text":"The adapter's constants — "},{"id":"spn-69668","marks":["code"],"text":"directed"},{"id":"spn-69669","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69670","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-69671","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69672","marks":["code"],"text":"signal"},{"id":"spn-69673","text":", the frozen port pairs — are V1's elisions. Applied to an artifact of a later version whose elisions differ, they would not fail; they would produce confident, wrong relations."}]},{"id":"blk-42108","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const V1_IR_VERSIONS = deepFreeze([\"1.0\", \"1.1\"]);\nexport function assertV1Artifact(artifact)   // → WRL_UNSUPPORTED_IR_VERSION"},{"id":"blk-42109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69674","text":"Called before any edge is read, on both the single-world and the correspondence paths."}]},{"id":"blk-42110","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69675","marks":["bold"],"text":"Check."},{"id":"spn-69676","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69677","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/an-unknown-ir-version-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-69678","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-42111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69679","marks":["bold"],"text":"Flagged:"},{"id":"spn-69680","text":" I admitted "},{"id":"spn-69681","marks":["code"],"text":"\"1.1\""},{"id":"spn-69682","text":" alongside "},{"id":"spn-69683","marks":["code"],"text":"\"1.0\""},{"id":"spn-69684","text":" because the frozen corpus contains both and the elisions are identical across them. If you consider that too permissive — i.e. that the adapter should be pinned to exactly the versions whose elisions it has been "},{"id":"spn-69685","marks":["italic"],"text":"tested"},{"id":"spn-69686","text":" against — say so and I will narrow it."}]},{"id":"blk-42112","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69687","text":"5. Deep-frozen identity tables"}]},{"id":"blk-42113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69688","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-69689","text":" Every exported vocabulary was an ordinary array or object."}]},{"id":"blk-42114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69690","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-69691","text":" You reversed "},{"id":"spn-69692","marks":["code"],"text":"ENDPOINT_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-69693","text":" and widened "},{"id":"spn-69694","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-69695","text":" after import, and canonicalisation obligingly produced a different id for the same relation and admitted roles §D8 forbids. The role enumeration is not merely a list — it is the "},{"id":"spn-69696","marks":["bold"],"text":"sort key"},{"id":"spn-69697","text":" of the canonical form. A closed enumeration a consumer can reopen is an open enumeration with a comment attached."}]},{"id":"blk-42115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69698","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-69699","text":" A recursive "},{"id":"spn-69700","marks":["code"],"text":"deepFreeze"},{"id":"spn-69701","text":" applied to every exported table: "},{"id":"spn-69702","marks":["code"],"text":"ENDPOINT_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-69703","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69704","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATIONS"},{"id":"spn-69705","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69706","marks":["code"],"text":"TEXTURES"},{"id":"spn-69707","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69708","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-69709","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69710","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-69711","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69712","marks":["code"],"text":"ALLOCATION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-69713","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69714","marks":["code"],"text":"PROFILE_DEFAULT_DOMAIN"},{"id":"spn-69715","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69716","marks":["code"],"text":"V1_IR_VERSIONS"},{"id":"spn-69717","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69718","marks":["code"],"text":"RELATION_IMPORTED_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-69719","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69720","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-69721","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-42116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69722","marks":["bold"],"text":"Check."},{"id":"spn-69723","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69724","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/immutability/the-canon-cannot-be-moved-from-outside"},{"id":"spn-69725","text":" — tampers with all of them, then re-asserts canonical order "},{"id":"spn-69726","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-69727","text":" role legality. It checks the consequence, not the "},{"id":"spn-69728","marks":["code"],"text":"Object.isFrozen"},{"id":"spn-69729","text":" flag."}]},{"id":"blk-42117","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69730","text":"6. Correspondence separated from "},{"id":"spn-69731","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"}]},{"id":"blk-42118","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69732","text":"This is the item I think was most valuable, and I want to state the general rule rather than just the fix."}]},{"id":"blk-42119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69733","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-69734","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69735","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-69736","text":" returned a field called "},{"id":"spn-69737","marks":["code"],"text":"imported"},{"id":"spn-69738","text":", whose entries had the four fields of a "},{"id":"spn-69739","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-69740","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-42120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69741","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-69742","text":" The arithmetic was fine. What was wrong is that a "},{"id":"spn-69743","marks":["italic"],"text":"derivation"},{"id":"spn-69744","text":" produced a record whose entire content is "},{"id":"spn-69745","marks":["italic"],"text":"an operation was accepted"},{"id":"spn-69746","text":" — from two artifacts, which know nothing about operations. Read strictly it says two worlds are related by a migration because they contain matching edge keys, so two unrelated worlds built from the same starter template would be full of imports nobody performed."}]},{"id":"blk-42121","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69747","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-69748","text":" Three functions where there was one:"}]},{"id":"blk-42122","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"deriveLegacyEdgeCorrespondence(from, to)  // structural, derived: { pairs, dropped, added }\ncandidateImportedFacts(correspondence)    // what a fact would have to be backed by\ncheckRelationImported(facts, corr)        // the join → WRL_UNVERIFIED_IMPORT"},{"id":"blk-42123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69749","marks":["bold"],"text":"The rule underneath it."},{"id":"spn-69750","text":" Derived values do not need checking against their own inputs; "},{"id":"spn-69751","marks":["bold"],"text":"asserted"},{"id":"spn-69752","text":" ones do. "},{"id":"spn-69753","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-69754","text":" is emitted by an accepted migration operation, which makes it — uniquely in this kernel — a thing that can be "},{"id":"spn-69755","marks":["italic"],"text":"maintained wrongly"},{"id":"spn-69756","text":", which is exactly why it is the one thing joined against something derived. Merging the two loses the only join that could catch a wrong assertion, and loses it by making the assertion "},{"id":"spn-69757","marks":["bold"],"text":"unfalsifiable"},{"id":"spn-69758","text":" rather than by making it false."}]},{"id":"blk-42124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69759","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-69760","text":" "},{"id":"spn-69761","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"},{"id":"spn-69762","text":" (asserts "},{"id":"spn-69763","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-69764","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-69765","marks":["italic"],"text":"gone"},{"id":"spn-69766","text":", that no "},{"id":"spn-69767","marks":["code"],"text":"imported"},{"id":"spn-69768","text":" key exists, and that a pair entry's keys are exactly "},{"id":"spn-69769","marks":["code"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-69770","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-69771","marks":["code"],"text":"from_relation"},{"id":"spn-69772","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-69773","marks":["code"],"text":"to_relation"},{"id":"spn-69774","text":"), "},{"id":"spn-69775","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-unbacked-import-fact-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-69776","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69777","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/the-fact-has-exactly-four-fields"},{"id":"spn-69778","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-42125","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69779","marks":["code"],"text":"playground.html"},{"id":"spn-69780","text":" was updated to the new API and re-verified live — it renders "},{"id":"spn-69781","marks":["code"],"text":"3 paired · 1 dropped · 0 added"},{"id":"spn-69782","text":" against the pinned fixture."}]},{"id":"blk-42126","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69783","text":"7. Empty-world correspondence"}]},{"id":"blk-42127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69784","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-empty-world-still-corresponds-to-itself"},{"id":"spn-69785","text":" — a world with no relations mapped against itself reports "},{"id":"spn-69786","marks":["code"],"text":"identityPreserved: true"},{"id":"spn-69787","text":" with all three lists empty. This is the degenerate case a correspondence that fails by returning nothing would be "},{"id":"spn-69788","marks":["bold"],"text":"indistinguishable"},{"id":"spn-69789","text":" from, which is why you asked for it and why the other migration checks do not cover it. Verified live in the playground on the \"Empty world\" preset as well."}]},{"id":"blk-42128","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69790","text":"8. The missing model-register rows, and the B7 re-stage"}]},{"id":"blk-42129","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69791","text":"The register went "},{"id":"spn-69792","marks":["bold"],"text":"34 → 47 rows"},{"id":"spn-69793","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-69794","marks":["code"],"text":"model · executable"},{"id":"spn-69795","text":" went "},{"id":"spn-69796","marks":["bold"],"text":"22 → 35"},{"id":"spn-69797","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-69798","marks":["code"],"text":"model · awaiting"},{"id":"spn-69799","text":" remains "},{"id":"spn-69800","marks":["bold"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-69801","text":", so the "},{"id":"spn-69802","marks":["code"],"text":"REGISTERED_MODEL_DEBT_CAP = 0"},{"id":"spn-69803","text":" ratchet holds."}]},{"id":"blk-42130","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69804","text":"8a. The B7 split you ordered"}]},{"id":"blk-42131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69805","text":"Two rows were "},{"id":"spn-69806","marks":["italic"],"text":"half"},{"id":"spn-69807","text":" misfiled, and I think this is the sharpest instance of the register's own failure mode that has come up:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-42133","spans":[{"id":"spn-69808","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-42134","spans":[{"id":"spn-69809","text":"was"}]},{"id":"blk-42135","spans":[{"id":"spn-69810","text":"is now"}]}],"id":"blk-42132","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-42136","spans":[{"id":"spn-69811","marks":["code"],"text":"same-name-different-world-differs"}]},{"id":"blk-42137","spans":[{"id":"spn-69812","text":"surface · awaiting"}]},{"id":"blk-42138","spans":[{"id":"spn-69813","marks":["bold"],"text":"split"},{"id":"spn-69814","text":": "},{"id":"spn-69815","marks":["code"],"text":"named-allocation-is-world-scoped"},{"id":"spn-69816","text":" (model · executable) + itself, narrowed, still surface · awaiting"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42139","spans":[{"id":"spn-69817","marks":["code"],"text":"overlapping-grants-do-not-collide"}]},{"id":"blk-42140","spans":[{"id":"spn-69818","text":"runtime · awaiting"}]},{"id":"blk-42141","spans":[{"id":"spn-69819","marks":["bold"],"text":"split"},{"id":"spn-69820","text":": "},{"id":"spn-69821","marks":["code"],"text":"granted-allocation-separates-grants"},{"id":"spn-69822","text":" (model · executable) + itself, narrowed, still runtime · awaiting"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-42142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69823","text":"Both were filed correctly "},{"id":"spn-69824","marks":["italic"],"text":"as far as it went"},{"id":"spn-69825","text":" — there is no syntax for naming a relation and no machinery for issuing a grant. But an identity is a function of a "},{"id":"spn-69826","marks":["bold"],"text":"preimage"},{"id":"spn-69827","text":", and both preimages are writable today: a "},{"id":"spn-69828","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69829","text":" carries its "},{"id":"spn-69830","marks":["code"],"text":"world_id"},{"id":"spn-69831","text":", a "},{"id":"spn-69832","marks":["code"],"text":"GrantedAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69833","text":" carries its "},{"id":"spn-69834","marks":["code"],"text":"grant_id"},{"id":"spn-69835","text":". The arithmetic was never blocked; only the way a "},{"id":"spn-69836","marks":["italic"],"text":"person"},{"id":"spn-69837","text":" reaches it was. A single row covering both had the effect of hiding a settled property behind an unsettled one, and reported "},{"id":"spn-69838","marks":["bold"],"text":"less"},{"id":"spn-69839","text":" than was known."}]},{"id":"blk-42143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69840","text":"This is what forced the three-authorities separation:"}]},{"id":"blk-42144","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69841","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which variants exist"},{"id":"spn-69842","text":" — all three. "},{"id":"spn-69843","marks":["code"],"text":"relationIdFromAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69844","text":" mints any"}]}],"id":"blk-42145","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-42147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69845","text":"well-formed allocation, and mints it the same way for everyone."}]},{"id":"blk-42148","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69846","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which a trusted importer may construct"},{"id":"spn-69847","text":" — only "},{"id":"spn-69848","marks":["code"],"text":"legacy-edge"},{"id":"spn-69849","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-42149","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69850","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which an authoring surface may emit"},{"id":"spn-69851","text":" — none, today."}]}],"id":"blk-42151","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-42153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69852","marks":["code"],"text":"assertImportableAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69853","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-69854","marks":["code"],"text":"assertAuthorableAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69855","text":" are separate boundaries; the mint refuses nothing. Folding them into the hash, as 0.1.1 did, made identity depend on "},{"id":"spn-69856","marks":["bold"],"text":"who was asking"},{"id":"spn-69857","text":" — which is the property a content address exists to not have."}]},{"id":"blk-42154","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69858","text":"8b. The other new rows"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-42156","spans":[{"id":"spn-69859","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-42157","spans":[{"id":"spn-69860","text":"check"}]}],"id":"blk-42155","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-42158","spans":[{"id":"spn-69861","marks":["code"],"text":"directed-carries-a-texture"}]},{"id":"blk-42159","spans":[{"id":"spn-69862","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/directed-carries-a-texture"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42160","spans":[{"id":"spn-69863","marks":["code"],"text":"texture-vocabulary-is-closed"}]},{"id":"blk-42161","spans":[{"id":"spn-69864","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/texture-vocabulary-is-the-specs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42162","spans":[{"id":"spn-69865","marks":["code"],"text":"declared-vocabularies-are-immutable"}]},{"id":"blk-42163","spans":[{"id":"spn-69866","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/immutability/the-canon-cannot-be-moved-from-outside"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42164","spans":[{"id":"spn-69867","marks":["code"],"text":"allocation-variants-have-declared-fields"}]},{"id":"blk-42165","spans":[{"id":"spn-69868","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/allocations/each-variant-has-exactly-its-declared-fields"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42166","spans":[{"id":"spn-69869","marks":["code"],"text":"relation-id-binds-to-the-artifact-it-claims"}]},{"id":"blk-42167","spans":[{"id":"spn-69870","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/a-forged-world-id-is-refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42168","spans":[{"id":"spn-69871","marks":["code"],"text":"world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"}]},{"id":"blk-42169","spans":[{"id":"spn-69872","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/the-world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42170","spans":[{"id":"spn-69873","marks":["code"],"text":"import-admits-only-declared-artifact-versions"}]},{"id":"blk-42171","spans":[{"id":"spn-69874","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/an-unknown-ir-version-is-refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42172","spans":[{"id":"spn-69875","marks":["code"],"text":"an-empty-world-corresponds-to-itself"}]},{"id":"blk-42173","spans":[{"id":"spn-69876","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-empty-world-still-corresponds-to-itself"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42174","spans":[{"id":"spn-69877","marks":["code"],"text":"a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"}]},{"id":"blk-42175","spans":[{"id":"spn-69878","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-42176","spans":[{"id":"spn-69879","marks":["code"],"text":"an-import-fact-is-backed-by-a-pairing"}]},{"id":"blk-42177","spans":[{"id":"spn-69880","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-unbacked-import-fact-is-refused"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-42178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69881","text":"Four existing rows had their "},{"id":"spn-69882","marks":["bold"],"text":"wording"},{"id":"spn-69883","text":" corrected rather than their status, because they were describing behaviour this commit changed: "},{"id":"spn-69884","marks":["code"],"text":"revision-does-not-move-relation-id"},{"id":"spn-69885","text":" (partition is now 2/1/4), "},{"id":"spn-69886","marks":["code"],"text":"import-supplies-only-declared-constants"},{"id":"spn-69887","text":" (adds the "},{"id":"spn-69888","marks":["italic"],"text":"resolved"},{"id":"spn-69889","text":" class; texture is no longer \"a missing key, never a null\"), "},{"id":"spn-69890","marks":["code"],"text":"import-mints-one-allocation-variant"},{"id":"spn-69891","text":" (the refusal moved from the mint to the two writer boundaries), "},{"id":"spn-69892","marks":["code"],"text":"migration-correspondence-is-derivable"},{"id":"spn-69893","text":" (no longer calls the derived pairing a "},{"id":"spn-69894","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-69895","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-42179","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69896","text":"9. What I need from you"}]},{"id":"blk-42180","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69897","text":"9a. Two decisions I took autonomously"}]},{"id":"blk-42181","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69898","marks":["bold"],"text":"`V1_IR_VERSIONS = [\"1.0\", \"1.1\"]`"},{"id":"spn-69899","text":" — see §4. Narrow it if you disagree."}]}],"id":"blk-42182","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69900","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-69901","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_version"},{"id":"spn-69902","text":" and profile are checked; the "},{"id":"spn-69903","marks":["italic"],"text":"rulepack"},{"id":"spn-69904","text":" is not.** The adapter"}]}],"id":"blk-42184","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-42186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69905","text":"reads "},{"id":"spn-69906","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_policies.rulepack_id"},{"id":"spn-69907","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-69908","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"},{"id":"spn-69909","text":" without validating it against a declared set, on the grounds that "},{"id":"spn-69910","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"},{"id":"spn-69911","text":" is the one "},{"id":"spn-69912","marks":["bold"],"text":"free"},{"id":"spn-69913","text":" field and so cannot reach an id. That is true today and stops being true the moment anything else consumes it. I left it, and I am flagging it rather than quietly relying on it."}]},{"id":"blk-42187","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69914","text":"9b. Path B — "},{"id":"spn-69915","marks":["bold"],"text":"answered, and built"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69916","text":"The two questions below were the ones I could not answer myself. You ruled both, and Path B is now built to that ruling: "},{"id":"spn-69917","marks":["code"],"text":"relations"},{"id":"spn-69918","text":" replaces "},{"id":"spn-69919","marks":["code"],"text":"edges"},{"id":"spn-69920","text":" outright at V2, §D8.8's projection is the V1 compatibility adapter only, and "},{"id":"spn-69921","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69922","text":"'s surface landed "},{"id":"spn-69923","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside"},{"id":"spn-69924","text":" B as slice B.4. Slices B.1 – B.5 are green at 828/828 with model debt 0. "},{"id":"spn-69925","marks":["bold"],"text":"See `HANDOFF_D8_PATH_B.md`"},{"id":"spn-69926","text":" — this section is left standing as the record of where Path A stopped."}]}],"id":"blk-42188","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-42190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69927","text":"I have your B1–B7 rulings. Path A is now closed on my side and I can start B under the byte-layout rulings, but B is a Semantic IR "},{"id":"spn-69928","marks":["bold"],"text":"V2"},{"id":"spn-69929","text":" design task, and the two things I do not have are:"}]},{"id":"blk-42191","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69930","text":"the V2 byte layout ruled at the level of detail A had — specifically: does the"}]}],"id":"blk-42192","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-42194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69931","marks":["code"],"text":"relations"},{"id":"spn-69932","text":" array replace "},{"id":"spn-69933","marks":["code"],"text":"edges"},{"id":"spn-69934","text":" outright at V2 or coexist with it, and does the frozen legacy projection of §D8.8 remain "},{"id":"spn-69935","marks":["bold"],"text":"normative"},{"id":"spn-69936","text":" at V2 or become a read-only import path?"}]},{"id":"blk-42195","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-42197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69937","text":"whether the surface for "},{"id":"spn-69938","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-69939","text":" lands "},{"id":"spn-69940","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside"},{"id":"spn-69941","text":" B or after it."}]}],"id":"blk-42196","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-42198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69942","text":"B7's split leaves one "},{"id":"spn-69943","marks":["code"],"text":"surface · awaiting"},{"id":"spn-69944","text":" row that only a surface can close, and I would rather not invent naming syntax to close a register row."}]},{"id":"blk-42199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69945","text":"Everything in this memo is committed as one A.3 closure commit inside "},{"id":"spn-69946","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL/"},{"id":"spn-69947","text":" (own repo "},{"id":"spn-69948","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/WRL"},{"id":"spn-69949","text":", branch "},{"id":"spn-69950","marks":["code"],"text":"main"},{"id":"spn-69951","text":") — per your ruling, \"after that battery is green and the pinned V1 IDs remain unchanged\"."}]},{"id":"blk-42200","kind